{
  "abstract": "Quadratic ideal-pair correlations involve class-dependent denominators, common ideals and real unit windows. We give explicit arithmetic bounds for this measure, including a signed estimate for the pure selected/conjugate kernel with selected modulus exceeding the shift interval. Let $m$ be an odd squarefree split modulus, $k=\\omega(m)$, $\\delta=\\varphi(m)/m$, $V\\ge T\\ge1$, and let the shifts be an interval of length $N$ or its units modulo $m$, with $N\\delta\\ge2^{k+1}$. For the flat nonrational lag average with denominator norm coprime to $m$, we prove the bound $E(V,T)\\{12\\delta^{-1}V2^k/m+4\\delta^{-1}\\sqrt{V/T}+[256V2^k\\sqrt m(1+\\log m)+32V3^k]/(\\delta^2N)\\}$, where $E(V,T)=\\mathcal D(VT)\\mathcal D(T)(1+\\log T)$ and $\\mathcal D(X)=\\max_{n\\le X}\\tau(n)$. Exact integral trace coordinates make the lag polynomial's discriminant a square. A trace-divisibility count controls its exceptional complete means; separating degenerate primes permits square-root completion using the classical Kloosterman bound. We retain the trace-zero row, actual unit-shift autocorrelations and real sign changes. In a specified range with $\\log\\log D\\ge100000$ and $D^{1/25000}\\le m\\le D^{1/240}$, the signed bound is at most $UD^{-117/10^7}$ after an additional $4^{\\omega(D)}$. Companion results control denominator replacement, both norm-resonance signs, norm-congruence tails and large common ideals, uniformly over classes and regulators. Exact arithmetic and 192-bit interval checks support the proofs and test omitted exceptional cases; they do not reprove the imported Kloosterman theorem. Bounded lag-independent factors are allowed; lag-dependent residual ray factors and the full orientation-family transfer remain unresolved. No new discriminant endpoint or field census is claimed.",
